    '<div class="card"><div class="hd"><div><span class="kicker">Kept from Databook, in full</span><h3>Everything Databook already has</h3></div></div><div class="gx-keeps">' + ['Customer context graph', 'Entity resolution', 'Risk threads with provenance', 'Guided plays and coaches', 'Smart templates', 'AI Studio and the agent composer', 'The 22 workflows', 'Closed-loop analytics', 'Outcome-based pricing', 'Forward-deployed engineers'].map((x) => '<span>' + x + '</span>').join('') + '</div></div>' +
    '<div class="card"><div class="hd"><div><span class="kicker">What starts first</span><h3>The first 30 days</h3></div><span class="hd-r"><button class="linkbtn" data-act="tab" data-t="deploy">The full deployment plan</button></span></div><ol class="gx-30"><li><b>Name an owner for every source.</b> One person accountable for Salesforce, Gong, monday.com, Grafana and the outside data, with a refresh and a place to fix it.</li><li><b>Baseline before anything changes.</b> Three leading measures and one outcome, with the CFO\'s plan as the baseline.</li><li><b>Agree Zoom\'s stage criteria.</b> Sales operations writes what should exist at each stage, so the methodology check has something to check.</li><li><b>Set the adoption gates.</b> What share of sellers must be active before a second region joins.</li><li><b>Pick two to four workflows.</b> The ones that solve a problem Zoom has today.</li></ol></div>';
